k in  july  while the lakers were still trying to  wait out kawhi leonard when they had  like unofficially three players on the  roster when it was  anthony davis lebron james and kyle  kuzma you  we both know that winning a championship  is more than just top level talent  now all the laker moves that they made  that rob palinka made  they worked out brilliantly but do not  anyone  sit here and tell me that you were sure  about any of these patchwork decisions  uh in september or even october who  deserves the most credit  for the lakers as champions this year  uh you always got to start with lebron  um  and not just because of the numbers and  the performance on the floor but you  heard  several laker players you heard rob  palinka allude to this  last night that labrador ship  in the bubble was invaluable and i guess  you could even perceive that his  leadership and kind of patching this  team together early on  and making it a cohesive unit was big  and then you get down to the bubble and  all the trying circumstances to have a  leader like lebron james in that mix  i i don't think you could put it you  know i don't think you can calculate  exactly how much that's worth so not  only was he producing  at an extremely high level a  ridiculously high level  for a player his age at this stage of  his career but what he did off the  court was clearly influential with not  to the lakers success  i'm trying to find the negative today  because somebody's going to find the  negative with lebron  and and i was wondering if they were  going to say well  it was an easier road in the bubble  which i don't believe  or lebron after the game saying  i want my damn respect like i'm just  trying to figure out so help me  understand  how us talking heads are going to spin  this a different way  from lebron james in the lakers i i  don't know how you do that  like it's not that's  bronze fault that the clippers fizzled  out in the second round  it's not lebron's fault that the bucks  didn't hold up their end of the bargain  in getting to the finals this isn't  boxing you play who's in front of you  you don't get to choose  who your opponents are and the lakers  did that and you know gentlemen swept  their way through the  western conference finals and you know  needed six games to get rid of miami so  i don't look at the schedule  as as you can't look at that as a  negative you can't uh you know pin that  on  lebron james and look dan i wrote last  night  nothing will ever top what lebron  accomplished in cleveland  i mean that will always be the pinnacle  of his career not just because he  brought a championship to cleveland but  the circumstances in which he did it to  come back from 3-1 down against the you  know  greatest team in nba history at least in  the regular season  that will always be number one this to  me  is number two like this right here what  he did  uh in this season with this group in  this bubble in this harsh environment  and it was a harsh  environment it's not an easy place to go  and win a championship what he did there  this will rank as the second most  significant team accomplishment  in lebron james career anyone that tells  you otherwise uh just has  some kind of bone to pick with lebron  james we're talking to chris mannix  senior nba writer for sports illustrated  his most recent column there will  always be a goat debate but lebron james  has made a compelling case that there  shouldn't be  on james and other final masterpiece  yeah i don't want to get into the  greatest of all time because nobody ever  changes their opinion have you ever been  around somebody where you have a  discussion about this  and they go oh you know what on second  it's like politics people just don't  change their mind people are firmly  entrenched in this  i always just caution people appreciate  what you're seeing  because you will not see this he doesn't  miss playoff games  he wins he's he has hit more clutch  shots than anybody 